## Why This Is Asked
Tests weighted interval scheduling with an exact k constraint and reconstruction; requires sorting, precomputing p(i), and a 2D DP with backtracking; also considerations for memory optimization.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling
- DP with an extra dimension for exact k selections
- Precomputing p(i) (latest non-overlapping job)
- Space-time tradeoffs; backtracking reconstruction
- Stability under large n and k; edge-case handling when K > possible non-overlapping sets

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKNonOverlapping(jobs, K) {
  // jobs: {s, e, r}; sort by end time
  jobs.sort((a,b)=> a.e - b.e);
  const n = jobs.length;
  const end = jobs.map(j=> j.e);
  // p(i): last index < i with end[p] < start[i]
  const p = new Array(n).fill(-1);
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) {
    let lo=0, hi=i-1, ans=-1;
    while (lo<=hi){
      const mid=(lo+hi)>>1;
      if (end[mid] < jobs[i].s){ ans=mid; lo=mid+1; } else hi=mid-1;
    }
    p[i]=ans;
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(false));
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    for (let t=1; t<=K; t++){
      const without = dp[i-1][t];
      const withTake = (p[i-1] >= 0 ? dp[p[i-1]+1][t-1] : (t-1===0?0: -Infinity)) + jobs[i-1].r;
      if (withTake > without){ dp[i][t] = withTake; take[i][t] = true; } else { dp[i][t] = without; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction
  const res = [];
  let i=n, t=K;
  while (i>0 && t>0){
    if (take[i][t]){ res.push(i-1); i = (p[i-1] >= 0 ? p[i-1]+1 : 0); t--; }
    else { i--; }
  }
  res.reverse();
  return { revenue: dp[n][K], indices: res };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to an "at most K" constraint?
- How can you optimize memory to O(n + K) or O(K) and still reconstruct the solution?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with subarray composition where each block incurs a fixed cost, a realistic pattern in scheduling/payments. It also checks reconstruction of intervals.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums to compute subarray sums fast
- DP over positions and block counts
- Optimization: collapse inner max with a running best value per t
- Backpointer reconstruction for endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraySumMinusC(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const endAt = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = Array(k+1).fill(-1e15);
  const bestIdx = Array(k+1).fill(-1);
  bestVal[1] = 0; bestIdx[1] = 1; // allow start at 1 for first block
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      const endVal = pref[i] - c + bestVal[t];
      if (dp[i-1][t] >= endVal) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      } else {
        dp[i][t] = endVal;
        endAt[i][t] = {start: bestIdx[t], end: i};
      }
    }
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      const cand = dp[i][t-1] - pref[i];
      if (cand > bestVal[t]) { bestVal[t] = cand; bestIdx[t] = i+1; }
    }
  }
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const e = endAt[i][t];
    if (e) { blocks.push([e.start, e.end]); i = e.start - 1; t--; }
    else { i--; }
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

